Ladybird snaps a sticky box where its exact position lands, rather
than rounding its sticky offset and its position separately. Blink
does the same: FragmentPaintPropertyTreeBuilder::
UpdateStickyTranslation() rounds pixel_snap_offset plus
StickyPositionOffset() together. Gecko’s StickyScrollContainer::
PositionContinuations() moves the frame itself by the sticky
translation. And WebKit’s RenderLayer::updateLayerPosition() adds
offsetForInFlowPosition() to the layer’s location, so both of them
snap the box’s final position once.
